  <!-- Page Header -->
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>CPE Info</h1>
      <p class="page-header-subtitle">How your chapter activities count toward ISC2 credential renewal.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">The basics</span>
      <h2>CPEs keep your credential active</h2>
      <p>ISC2 credentials need CPE credits to stay active. CISSP needs <strong>40 a year</strong>; other credentials are similar. A chunk of those can come from chapter activities, and some people don't realize it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 24+ highlight -->
  <section class="content-section" style="background: var(--light-gray);">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">What you earn with us</span>
      <h2>About 24 CPEs a year from the chapter alone</h2>
      <p>Four quarterly meetings (4–6 CPEs each) plus BSides Tampa (8) lands somewhere between <strong>24 and 32 Group A CPEs</strong> for the year. That's more than half of what CISSP renewal needs, and you haven't counted any outside conference, webinar, or self-study yet. Add a chapter talk, a mentorship session, or a study group, and the whole year can come from the chapter.</p>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <p style="margin:0;">You don't have to self-report for chapter meetings or BSides. The chapter submits CPE credits on your behalf after each event.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Group A vs B -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">The two buckets</span>
      <h2>Group A vs Group B</h2>
      <p>ISC2 sorts CPEs into two buckets:</p>
      <ul class="benefits-list">
        <li><strong>Group A</strong> — directly related to your credential's domains. Security conferences, chapter meetings, teaching, writing, and reviewing security content.</li>
        <li><strong>Group B</strong> — general professional development that isn't specific to your credential's domains (for example, presentation skills courses).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Most chapter activities qualify as <strong>Group A</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What counts -->
  <section class="content-section" style="background: var(--light-gray);">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">The table</span>
      <h2>What counts</h2>

      <div class="cpe-table-wrapper">
        <table class="cpe-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Activity</th><th>Credit (Group A)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Attending a quarterly chapter meeting</td><td><strong>4&ndash;6</strong> per meeting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>BSides Tampa &mdash; conference day</td><td><strong>8</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>BSides Tampa &mdash; training day (Friday)</td><td>Varies by session</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Speaking at a chapter meeting</td><td>Prep + delivery hours</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Volunteering at BSides Tampa</td><td>Per hour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Running or participating in a study group</td><td>Per hour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Serving as a chapter officer</td><td>Per ISC2 chapter officer policy</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted-text);">Exact per-activity credit values come from the current <a href="https://www.isc2.org/-/media/ISC2/Certifications/CPE/CPE---Handbook.ashx">ISC2 CPE Handbook</a>. Always check against the latest version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to report -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Reporting</span>
      <h2>How to report other CPEs</h2>
      <p>For chapter meetings and BSides, we handle reporting. For everything else (outside conferences, webinars, self-study, speaking gigs), you submit it yourself:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Log into your ISC2 member dashboard at <a href="https://www.isc2.org/">isc2.org</a>.</li>
        <li>Go to <strong>CPEs &rarr; Submit CPE</strong>.</li>
        <li>Pick the Group (A or B) and the activity type.</li>
        <li>Enter the date, hours, and a short description.</li>
        <li>For chapter activities you're submitting yourself, reference "ISC2 Tampa Bay Chapter" and the event date. If ISC2 audits the claim, we can confirm attendance.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

